# `DfoBuilder::with_pso_config`

[Back to `dfo::DfoBuilder`](../DfoBuilder.md)

Sets the settings of the particle swarm method.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::DfoBuilder dfo::DfoBuilder::with_pso_config(const dfo::ParticleSwarmConfig &cfg) const;
```

## What It Does

Sets `DfoOptions::particle_swarm`, a [`ParticleSwarmConfig`](../ParticleSwarmConfig.md) that carries every setting of the particle swarm method. It is read only when that method runs, whether chosen by `Auto` or by [`with_solver`](with_solver.md). The common settings (budgets, tolerance, seed, display) and the bounds of the problem are applied on top of it when the method starts.

## Parameters

`const dfo::ParticleSwarmConfig &cfg`
: The particle swarm settings.

## Returns

A new builder with the change; the original is untouched.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The swarm size.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - pluss::series::make({1.0, -2.0, 0.5, 3.0})).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (1, -2, 0.5, 3)

  for (const std::int64_t n : {20, 100}) {
    dfo::ParticleSwarmConfig cfg;
    cfg.population_size = n;
    const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_solver(dfo::DfoSolverKind::ParticleSwarm).with_pso_config(cfg).solve();
    out.writeln("swarm", n, ": evaluations =", r.diagnostics.evaluations, ", minimum =", r.minimum);
  }
}
```

### Example 2

Cognitive and social pull.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - pluss::series::make({1.0, -2.0, 0.5, 3.0})).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (1, -2, 0.5, 3)

  dfo::ParticleSwarmConfig cfg;
  cfg.cognitive = 1.5;
  cfg.social = 1.5;
  const dfo::DfoBuilder base = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_solver(dfo::DfoSolverKind::ParticleSwarm);
  const dfo::DfoResult tuned = base.with_pso_config(cfg).solve(), plain = base.solve();
  out.writeln("defaults (2, 2): evaluations =", plain.diagnostics.evaluations, ", minimum =", plain.minimum);
  out.writeln("pull 1.5, 1.5  : evaluations =", tuned.diagnostics.evaluations, ", minimum =", tuned.minimum);
}
```

### Example 3

A velocity clamp.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - pluss::series::make({1.0, -2.0, 0.5, 3.0})).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (1, -2, 0.5, 3)

  dfo::ParticleSwarmConfig cfg;
  cfg.velocity_clamp_ratio = 0.2;
  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_solver(dfo::DfoSolverKind::ParticleSwarm).with_pso_config(cfg).solve();
  out.writeln("evaluations =", r.diagnostics.evaluations, ", minimum =", r.minimum);
}
```

